# Ephemeral, recipe-driven pulls -- never archived (DESIGN.md Sec 4). Re-fetchable
# on demand via bin/fetch_uniprot_proteome.py / bin/fetch_genome_assembly.py.
/data/
/logs/

# Same rule, per-study: a study's own data/ (e.g. a large reference database
# pull like Afumigatus_pangenome/data/starbase/*.sqlite) is class-1 ephemeral
# too, but /data/ above is root-anchored only and doesn't match nested paths
# -- caught 2026-09-17 before a ~365MB sqlite file was ever staged, same class
# of gap as studies/*/*/data_dir above.
studies/*/*/data/

# Per-study materialized inputs (decompressed FASTA/GFF3 built from data/ by
# bin/build_study_config.py) -- regenerable from species.csv + the cache above,
# not source. config.csv and DATA_MANIFEST.yaml (the actual tracked outputs of that
# script) are NOT excluded here since they're small and are the study's own record.
# No trailing slash: some studies share one study's data_dir via a symlink (e.g.
# a --cluster_tool comparison study reusing another's fetched data) rather than
# their own real directory, and a trailing-slash pattern only matches directories,
# not symlinks -- one such symlink (an absolute, host-specific path) was caught
# about to be committed for real on 2026-09-11 before this fix.
studies/*/*/data_dir

# Per-species UniProt DR annotation extracts (bin/extract_dat_annotations.py) --
# regenerable from the (also gitignored) data/uniprot/ cache in ~2s/species, not
# source.
studies/*/*/annotations/

# Nextflow run state (when studies invoke nf_NovInvenio directly from here)
.nextflow/
.nextflow.log*
work/
.nf_launch/

# results/view of pipeline runs -- regenerated fresh per DESIGN.md Sec 9, not archived
# except via docs/*/archive/ (small derived compressed TSVs, published deliberately).
# `results/*` (not `results/`) so a study's small, non-scaling summary report and
# figures (class 2 per CLAUDE.md's data-provenance rules -- fixed-size aggregate
# artifacts, not per-candidate/per-sequence output) can be explicitly un-ignored
# below; git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is itself excluded.
#
# Two patterns, not one: a pattern containing a non-trailing slash (like
# `results/*`) is anchored to the .gitignore's own location (the repo root),
# so it only ever matched a root-level results/ (used by bin/run_study.sh's
# main.nf-based `--outdir "$REPO_ROOT/results"` convention) -- it silently
# never covered a per-study `studies/<domain>/<set>/results/` (used by
# pangenome.nf-based studies' own run scripts), which is exactly the class-3
# per-candidate-scaling data this rule was meant to catch. Caught 2026-09-16
# when coccidioides_pangenome's results/ (20GB) and Afumigatus_pangenome's
# (14GB, pre-existing) both showed up untracked instead of ignored -- the
# `!studies/fungi/Afumigatus_pangenome/results/...` allowlist lines below
# were themselves dead no-ops until this fix, for the same reason.
/results/*
studies/*/*/results/*
view/
!studies/fungi/Afumigatus_pangenome/results/REPORT.md
!studies/fungi/Afumigatus_pangenome/results/SUMMARY.md
!studies/fungi/Afumigatus_pangenome/results/figures/
!studies/fungi/Afumigatus_pangenome/results/figures_pdf/

# TBLASTN alignment shards (nf_NovInvenio issue #73's BUILD_ALIGNMENT_SHARDS,
# relocated into the two-tier gallery path by bin/sync_reports.sh, issue #5) --
# unlike docs/*/archive/'s small TSVs, these carry real sequence text and can run
# into the multi-MB-gzipped range per genome (DESIGN.md Sec 8), so they are
# published as a GitHub Release asset (issue #1) instead of committed, and
# reassembled into docs/ only at Pages-deploy time (issue #2). Never committed
# even though they physically live under docs/ on local disk.
docs/*/*/alignments/
docs/*/*/loss_alignments/

# Report HTML/PDF (novelties/core/losses.html, summary.pdf) -- same reasoning as
# alignments/ above: these embed real candidate sequence text and grow with the
# data (one real case reached 105MB, over GitHub's 100MB file limit, 2026-09-10).
# Published as a GitHub Release asset (bin/publish_report_release.sh) instead of
# committed, merged into docs/ only at Pages-deploy time (.github/workflows/
# static.yml). report.html (the small, stable per-study landing page) and
# alignment.html (the small static viewer shell) are NOT part of this -- neither
# grows with candidate data, both stay git-tracked normally.
docs/*/*/novelties.html
docs/*/*/core.html
docs/*/*/losses.html
docs/*/*/summary.pdf

# Study/run layout (notes/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-study-run-site-layout-design.md):
# the same release-asset-only files one level down, in docs/<domain>/<study>/<run>/.
# The set-level rules above stay: old flat folders (and the temporary *_dmnd_*
# test folders) still hold real reports there. The only files committed at set
# level under these names are redirect stubs for old URLs, force-added by
# bin/migrate_docs_to_runs.py; tests/test_study_runs.py checks each one is a stub.
docs/*/*/*/novelties.html
docs/*/*/*/core.html
docs/*/*/*/losses.html
docs/*/*/*/summary.pdf
docs/*/*/*/alignments/
docs/*/*/*/loss_alignments/

# pangenome.nf runs publish one page per run at docs/<domain>/<set>/<run>/
# (bin/sync_pangenome_report.py). Only that run's report.html and run.json are
# committed. Figures are regenerated binaries; the tables and the synteny
# viewer grow with family/island count. All ship in the reports-* release
# asset and are merged into docs/ at Pages-deploy time (static.yml).
docs/*/*/*/figures/
docs/*/*/*/figures_pdf/
docs/*/*/*/archive/
docs/*/*/*/island_synteny.html
docs/*/*/*/assembly_quality.html

# pixi
.pixi/*
!.pixi/config.toml

# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Claude Code / mycelium session-local state
.claude/*.tmp
.claude/*.log
.claude/settings.local.json
.mycelium/locks/

# Local git worktrees (superpowers:using-git-worktrees)
.worktrees/

# BUSCO run output (regenerable; sordariales_shallow/busco/ is 3.9 GB, 28,908 files)
studies/*/*/busco/
# Tool logs from study scripts
studies/fungi/Afumigatus_pangenome/logs/
# Old flat pipeline docs/ output kept on disk after the study/run migration (not published)
studies/*/*/old_flat_docs_*/
